  "summary_en": "Mexico's Civil Aviation Law (1995, last reformed 14 Nov 2025) regulates airspace use, air transport concessions and permits, aircraft registration and airworthiness, personnel licensing, passenger rights and safety management. It includes limited provisions on unmanned, autonomous and remotely piloted aircraft (definitions, registration, certification by the Federal Civil Aviation Agency).",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Defines unmanned, autonomous and remotely piloted aircraft systems.",
   "AFAC issues technical-administrative rules for certification, operation and manufacture of civil and State unmanned aircraft (non-military).",
   "Remotely piloted aircraft systems not providing public service must be registered with AFAC.",
   "Service providers must implement safety management systems under the State Safety Program.",
   "Airworthiness certificates, insurance and registration are mandatory for aircraft operations."
  ],
